<DocsLayout
  title="ClipCut Documentation"
  description="Architecture, installation, AI providers, speech models, and production deployment for ClipCut."
  currentPath="/docs"
  section="Overview"
>
  <p>
    <strong>ClipCut</strong> is a free, MIT-licensed, self-hosted AI video clipping studio built with{" "}
    <strong>FastAPI</strong>, <strong>FFmpeg</strong>, <strong>yt-dlp</strong>,{" "}
    <strong>librosa</strong>, and local or cloud speech &amp; language models.
  </p>

  <h2>How the Pipeline Works</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>Ingestion:</strong> Paste a YouTube, Twitch, or Kick URL, upload a local file in
      resumable chunks, or monitor a live creator stream.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Transcription:</strong> Pulls existing captions via <code>youtube-transcript-api</code>{" "}
      or <code>yt-dlp</code> first, falling back to multi-language <code>faster-whisper</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Moment Detection &amp; Scoring:</strong> Tags vocal energy peaks with{" "}
      <code>librosa.feature.rms()</code>, attaches Most-Replayed viewer heatmaps, and scores hooks
      with your configured AI provider (or loudness fallback without a key).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Studio Editing &amp; Rendering:</strong> Renders <code>9:16</code>,{" "}
      <code>1:1</code>, or <code>16:9</code> clips with word-level ASS captions (<code>Bounce</code>,{" "}
      <code>Hype</code>, <code>Clean</code>) and background music sidechain auto-ducking.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Repository Map</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>studio/server.py</code> — FastAPI routes, auth/rate-limit middleware, media streaming</li>
    <li><code>studio/jobs.py</code> — Fair multi-user job queue and video pipeline orchestration</li>
    <li><code>studio/media.py</code> — <code>yt-dlp</code> ingestion, audio probing, and replay heatmaps</li>
    <li><code>studio/transcribe.py</code> — Multi-language ASR (<code>faster-whisper</code>, optional GPU worker)</li>
    <li><code>studio/brain.py</code> — Hook scoring prompts, gaming rules, and feedback personalization</li>
    <li><code>studio/render.py</code> — FFmpeg cutting, layouts, ASS captions, and BGM mixing</li>
    <li><code>web/index.html</code> — Single-file zero-build studio web application</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
